            "id": "weigh-three-timing-signals-and-choose-one-next-move",
            "title": "Weigh three timing signals and choose one next move",
            "do": "In the same answer, name the idea and its intended users. For technology, say what became possible and what was observed. For economics, name who has a reason to adopt, what cost or incentive changed, and what was observed. For readiness, say what the intended users already do and what behavior would have to change. Mark each condition observed, missing evidence, or contradicted; give its evidence or gap and what could change the verdict. Believe observations, not plausible stories. Wait for a stated condition if any prerequisite is contradicted. If none is contradicted but at least one lacks evidence, check the gap first. If all three are observed, propose one small reversible test. State why, the next move, and the observation that would reverse it. Return an internal plan only. Do not launch or commit resources.",
